WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.534
-Hi. I'm happy to be here.

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.234
I feel like
it's been a long time.

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:06.601
-It's been a while. By the way,
you smell fantastic, as well.

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:08.968
-Thank you.
I make it myself.

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:11.033
-Yeah -- Do you really?
-Yeah, because I get a headache

00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:12.534
from store-bought perfumes,

00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:14.067
so I just made it
with essential oils.

00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:15.868
-Oh, my gosh.
It's fantastic, whatever it is.

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:17.567
-It's like cooking, right?
-Yeah, I guess so.

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:20.100
By the way, speaking of cooking,
St. Patrick's Day is today.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:23.400
Irish cuisine --
not really that advanced.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.567
What would you --

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:26.767
[ Laughter ]
I can --

00:00:26.767 --> 00:00:29.033
I'm Irish. I can say
that we boil everything.

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:30.400
-Okay. Alright.
-We boil ev --

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.467
[Irish accent] What is it?
Eggs, oatmeal, whatever.

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:33.934
Boil it. Yeah.

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:36.033
I's like, "What? Corned beef?
Have you tried boiling it?"

00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:38.167
Yeah, it's like --
Cabbage -- we just boil it.

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:39.701
[Normal voice]
But what would you say --

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:41.400
What should people eat
on St. Patty's day?

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:42.934
-I mean, I'm not familiar --

00:00:42.934 --> 00:00:44.534
so familiar with Irish food,
believe it or not.

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:46.634
But I think something green,
right?

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:49.667
So have chlorophyll, which is
really good for your gut.

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:51.467
Like -- No, it's really good.

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:52.767
-Chlorophyll?
-Yes.

00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:53.767
-What are you talking about?
-Or, like, a green juice.

00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:55.400
Have a green juice.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.901
Maybe put some whiskey in it
'cause it's St. Patrick's day.

00:00:57.901 --> 00:01:00.234
-Now we're talking.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:01.934
-But eat your greens.
Eat your greens.

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:03.868
-Yeah. I was reading
a little bit about you.

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:07.634
And growing up in new York, one
of the things that you like --

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.100
'Cause I know --
I have your cookbooks.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:10.968
I watch you all the time
on all your cooking stuff,

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:12.634
besides "Top Chef."

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:15.100
And I found out that one of the
things that was a treat for you

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:17.534
growing up was to go
to the hot-dog cart.

00:01:17.534 --> 00:01:21.634
-Yes, but I didn't eat meat
then, so -- I mean, I -- Yes.

00:01:21.634 --> 00:01:24.234
We would actually --
I grew up in New York City.

00:01:24.234 --> 00:01:27.200
So my mom and I were vegetarian,
but we would always salivate

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.934
watching all these people
get hot dogs.

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:31.467
So we had the hot-dog --

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:33.601
We asked the hot-dog guy for the
hot dog without the hot dog.

00:01:33.601 --> 00:01:36.200
But all the fixings,
so, like, sauerkraut, onions,

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:40.300
mustard, relish, ketchup,
everything.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.767
It's good!

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.100
[ Laughter ]
It's really good!

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:44.834
That's what makes it taste good.

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:47.634
I mean, have you ever had
a New York hot dog boiled

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:49.200
in that New York water?

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.000
-[Irish accent]
Boiled? Ya say boiled?

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.434
Ha! Bingo!

00:01:53.434 --> 00:01:55.267
I love it!
-Exactly!

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:56.968
-[Normal voice] I actually
ordered one of the --

00:01:56.968 --> 00:01:58.734
-Oh, shoot.
-I ordered a Padma.

00:01:58.734 --> 00:02:00.133
-Aww.

00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:03.267
-This is the hot dog with
everything, with nothing.

00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:04.634
-Everything and nothing
all at once.

00:02:04.634 --> 00:02:06.200
-So it's everything
with nothing at once.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.601
You go, "Everything
with no hot dog."

00:02:07.601 --> 00:02:09.467
-Alright. We -- Can I --
Am I supposed to taste this?

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:11.534
-Yeah, do you want to?
-Yes, I do.

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:12.868
You made it for me.

00:02:12.868 --> 00:02:14.968
Alright, so, do you want
to make it more fun?

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.901
-Sure.
-Okay, should we have

00:02:16.901 --> 00:02:19.133
an eating contest and see
who can eat it faster?

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:20.334
-No.

00:02:20.334 --> 00:02:22.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:25.100
-Come on! Come on!

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.667
-Are you out of your mind? No.

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:28.901
I'm telling you --
I'm giving you the --

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:30.701
I will throw up
all over the place.

00:02:30.701 --> 00:02:32.400
I don't know
if I will like this.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.534
I don't think
I'm going to enjoy this.

00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:36.501
-You've had everything on here
before. I know you have.

00:02:36.501 --> 00:02:37.868
-It just doesn't seem --

00:02:37.868 --> 00:02:40.534
It seems like
it's missing something.

00:02:40.534 --> 00:02:41.734
Alright.
-Ready?

00:02:41.734 --> 00:02:43.167
-Cheers.
-One -- Cheers.

00:02:43.167 --> 00:02:47.868
♪♪

00:02:47.868 --> 00:02:49.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:52.000
-It's good. It's good.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.100
It has the hot sauce,
the red onions. This is good.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.300
Stop playing music, please.
Because --

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:58.968
Because they just want me
to eat it fast--

00:02:58.968 --> 00:03:00.601
who can eat it fast--
I'm not doing it.

00:03:00.601 --> 00:03:02.467
No, I don't want to do it.
-Oh, come on.

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:04.501
-But I feel like
it's the end of the hot dog

00:03:04.501 --> 00:03:06.267
when the hot dog
falls out of the bun

00:03:06.267 --> 00:03:08.667
and you have one bite left,
but you've already paid $1.50

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:09.934
for the hot dog.

00:03:09.934 --> 00:03:11.434
So you're like, "I might
as well finish the end."

00:03:11.434 --> 00:03:13.000
-Also look at your bite.
Your bite is small.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.901
-What are you talk--
What are you doing?

00:03:15.901 --> 00:03:17.934
You come out here
swinging like that?

00:03:17.934 --> 00:03:20.100
My bite is small?
-Come on.

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:23.701
-No, I don't want to eat this.
I really don't like this.

00:03:23.701 --> 00:03:27.200
I think this is -- this is
not -- this is not for me.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:28.334
-Okay, fine.

00:03:28.334 --> 00:03:29.901
-Do you want me
to take another bite?

00:03:29.901 --> 00:03:31.267
-Yeah.

00:03:31.267 --> 00:03:33.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:36.467
-I'll do anything for you.
-Thank you.

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:40.767
Keep going. Keep going.
Keep going!

00:03:40.767 --> 00:03:43.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:43.767 --> 00:03:48.334
♪♪

00:03:48.334 --> 00:03:50.300
You have the condiment sweats.

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:51.834
Not the meat sweats,
but the condiment sweats.

00:03:51.834 --> 00:03:53.400
-I was looking for any
spit bucket or anything.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.968
No one cares. No one cares.

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:57.667
No. I love you.
This is good. This is great.

00:03:57.667 --> 00:04:00.167
I would let you have all of it.

00:04:00.167 --> 00:04:01.667
Save it for you after the show.

00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:04.467
-Now I eat meat, obviously.
-You do, yeah.

00:04:04.467 --> 00:04:06.167
-I eat everything, you know,
with "Top Chef,"

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:08.000
but I'm still
pretty plant-based.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.300
-Can you -- Can you answer --

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:10.667
There are some food debates
that are online,

00:04:10.667 --> 00:04:12.567
and I thought
that it'd be fun answering these

00:04:12.567 --> 00:04:15.968
and just settling it
once and for all.

00:04:15.968 --> 00:04:18.200
Is a hot dog a sandwich
or a hot dog?

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.467
-I mean, it's a poor excuse
for a sandwich,

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:22.033
but it's technically a sandwich.

00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:23.734
Anything between bread.
[ Audience groans ]

00:04:23.734 --> 00:04:25.667
-This is --
The crowd turned on you.

00:04:25.667 --> 00:04:27.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:31.901
-I mean, in July, when you're
grilling the hot dog it's good,

00:04:31.901 --> 00:04:34.501
but not when you're boiling it.

00:04:34.501 --> 00:04:36.234
-What are you talking --
A hot dog is good, but I'm --

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:37.734
That's not the question --
"Is a hot dog good?"

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:38.868
-It is -- It is --

00:04:38.868 --> 00:04:40.067
-The answer is,
yes, the hot dog is good.

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:41.801
-Yes, it's technically
a sandwich.

00:04:41.801 --> 00:04:42.968
-What?

00:04:42.968 --> 00:04:44.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:46.367
-Anything --
because the Earl of Sandwich

00:04:46.367 --> 00:04:47.734
invented the sandwich.

00:04:47.734 --> 00:04:49.667
How far do you want me
to go with this?

00:04:49.667 --> 00:04:51.467
-The Earl of Sandwich.
-It's true.

00:04:51.467 --> 00:04:53.467
Alright. Ready?
Settle this debate.

00:04:53.467 --> 00:04:57.234
Is there a food that's not made
better with chocolate or ranch?

00:04:57.234 --> 00:04:58.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.701 --> 00:05:01.634
I would say...
not necessarily, right?

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:03.901
Have you ever had
a chocolate-covered something

00:05:03.901 --> 00:05:05.567
that was gross?
-Oh, hell yes, I have.

00:05:05.567 --> 00:05:08.000
And it was the worst thing
I've ever eaten on "Top Chef."

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.400
-Wait. Which one?
'Cause I watch all the --

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.100
-It was Ilan Hall.
-I love Ilan.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:12.601
-So do I.

00:05:12.601 --> 00:05:15.167
But he really tested me there.
It was in Santa Barbara.

00:05:15.167 --> 00:05:17.467
It was a --
-You remember the location.

00:05:17.467 --> 00:05:19.634
-I remember what I was wearing.

00:05:19.634 --> 00:05:21.267
It was this beautiful
chocolate ganache

00:05:21.267 --> 00:05:23.601
that he did really well,
and I bit into it

00:05:23.601 --> 00:05:25.601
and I thought it was a piece
of fruit or something

00:05:25.601 --> 00:05:27.734
because it kind of felt
like that or a raisin.

00:05:27.734 --> 00:05:29.801
It was a piece of liver.

00:05:29.801 --> 00:05:31.868
[ Audience groans ]
So chocolate-covered liver.

00:05:31.868 --> 00:05:33.901
Not good. It would have
been better with ranch.

00:05:33.901 --> 00:05:35.868
-Oh, my g-- Oh, my gosh.

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.200
Alright.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:40.334
If -- Are you cooking
if you don't use heat?

00:05:40.334 --> 00:05:43.701
-Yes, you are. You can marinate
things, and they will cook.

00:05:43.701 --> 00:05:46.167
Like, if you leave fish,
that's a ceviche.

00:05:46.167 --> 00:05:48.934
Yeah. I mean, we had this debate
on my first season,

00:05:48.934 --> 00:05:52.834
the second season finale
between Ilan, again, and Sam,

00:05:52.834 --> 00:05:55.100
and Sam marinated something,

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:57.334
and Tom was like,
"But he didn't cook anything!"

00:05:57.334 --> 00:05:59.100
And I'm like, "Yes, he did.
He just didn't use heat."

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:00.868
-Ah. Alright, So you
are cooking. I agree with that.

00:06:00.868 --> 00:06:02.367
Yeah, yeah.

00:06:02.367 --> 00:06:04.734
Could a bowl of cereal
be considered a soup?

00:06:04.734 --> 00:06:06.868
I don't know where
we're getting these.

00:06:06.868 --> 00:06:09.100
-Only if you're Questlove.
-I don't know where --

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:11.200
-Do you like --
-He loves cereal. Come on.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:12.734
-I do.
-What's your --

00:06:12.734 --> 00:06:14.467
What's your cereal?

00:06:14.467 --> 00:06:16.734
-I like Qu--
Do you know Quisp?

00:06:16.734 --> 00:06:18.701
-They don't make Quisp.

00:06:18.701 --> 00:06:20.100
-They got Quisp for my birthday.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:23.267
-They don't make Quisps.
-They still make it.

00:06:23.267 --> 00:06:27.067
-Where did you get
the last box of Quisp?

00:06:27.067 --> 00:06:31.367
-They -- For my birthday,
people sent me Quisp.

00:06:31.367 --> 00:06:33.033
-I was at his birthday,

00:06:33.033 --> 00:06:34.767
and he literally
had 20 boxes of cereal...

00:06:34.767 --> 00:06:36.934
-Oh, yeah, he does like cereal.
-...and every milk, yes.

00:06:36.934 --> 00:06:39.434
Like, did you know
there were Frosted Flakes

00:06:39.434 --> 00:06:41.000
that were strawberry?
Yeah.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.234
-No.
-They're great.

00:06:42.234 --> 00:06:44.133
-Oh, yeah.
He knows all that stuff.

00:06:44.133 --> 00:06:45.501
-He knows all that stuff.
-Oh, that's good. Yeah.

00:06:45.501 --> 00:06:47.033
But, no, it can't be considered
a soup. It's a cereal.

00:06:47.033 --> 00:06:49.501
-Yeah. Maybe it's a dessert
more than a soup.

00:06:49.501 --> 00:06:51.601
[ Audience murmurs ]

00:06:51.601 --> 00:06:54.868
The way you say it, true, of
course, probably, yeah, yeah.

00:06:54.868 --> 00:06:56.467
Can we talk
about "Top Chef," okay?

00:06:56.467 --> 00:06:58.601
-Yes, please.
-Season 20.

00:06:58.601 --> 00:07:00.400
Can you believe it's season 20?

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:03.467
-No, I can't. When I took
the job umpteen years ago --

00:07:03.467 --> 00:07:04.901
-We've known each other
for 20 years.

00:07:04.901 --> 00:07:06.033
-We have.
-Isn't that wild?

00:07:06.033 --> 00:07:07.200
-You look the same.
-You do.

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:08.534
You look younger and better.

00:07:08.534 --> 00:07:10.667
-[ Laughs ] Thank you.
It's all that food I eat.

00:07:10.667 --> 00:07:12.634
I mean, it's been
a really wild ride.

00:07:12.634 --> 00:07:15.100
I just took the job
because I thought it would be

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:16.367
a little push for my cookbook,

00:07:16.367 --> 00:07:17.968
which was coming out
the year of that.

00:07:17.968 --> 00:07:20.067
So you didn't think you'd go,
like, past two seasons?

00:07:20.067 --> 00:07:21.234
-No, it was a little cable show.

00:07:21.234 --> 00:07:22.634
I mean, I didn't do it
for a season,

00:07:22.634 --> 00:07:24.067
so I did get to see it,
and I thought

00:07:24.067 --> 00:07:25.667
it was a really cool show.
-Yeah.

00:07:25.667 --> 00:07:28.434
-And so I liked it.
I just, you know --

00:07:28.434 --> 00:07:31.067
I was talking to them about
the first season in development.

00:07:31.067 --> 00:07:34.534
Then I went off to shoot a movie
with Sean Bean, actually,

00:07:34.534 --> 00:07:35.801
and they didn't want to wait,

00:07:35.801 --> 00:07:37.133
so they did it
with somebody else.

00:07:37.133 --> 00:07:39.634
And then it was nice.
You know, it was a good show.

00:07:39.634 --> 00:07:41.100
And then they asked me,
second season,

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:42.567
"Are you free now?"
And I said, "Yes."

00:07:42.567 --> 00:07:44.067
And I've been with the show
ever since.

00:07:44.067 --> 00:07:46.400
-Wowzers. That's awesome.
Well, you're the face.

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:48.133
I couldn't imagine it
without you.

00:07:48.133 --> 00:07:49.934
-Thank you.
-You're so good.

00:07:49.934 --> 00:07:51.767
Talk to me about this season.
What is this now?

00:07:51.767 --> 00:07:53.634
This is very interesting,
'cause now it's --

00:07:53.634 --> 00:07:55.167
It's become global now,
"Top Chef."

00:07:55.167 --> 00:07:56.767
-Yeah, this is like
the mega season.

00:07:56.767 --> 00:07:58.501
It's hard to top yourself.
It's like an old marriage.

00:07:58.501 --> 00:08:00.234
When you've been on TV so long,

00:08:00.234 --> 00:08:02.834
you got to keep it fresh,
keep it, you know, exciting.

00:08:02.834 --> 00:08:05.133
So, this season,
it's really international.

00:08:05.133 --> 00:08:08.367
We always try to keep it
diverse, but we have --

00:08:08.367 --> 00:08:10.634
"Top Chef" is in
174 territories.

00:08:10.634 --> 00:08:12.767
So, like, I'm dubbed
in all kinds of languages,

00:08:12.767 --> 00:08:14.434
which is really funny to watch.

00:08:14.434 --> 00:08:17.701
But there are 29 countries where
they have their own franchise,

00:08:17.701 --> 00:08:23.467
so we took winners and finalists
from 11 of those.

00:08:23.467 --> 00:08:26.267
So, we have, like,
Brazil, Thailand,

00:08:26.267 --> 00:08:28.567
Mexico, Italy, the Middle East,

00:08:28.567 --> 00:08:30.234
you know, all these different
top chefs.

00:08:30.234 --> 00:08:31.400
-All the best.
-Yeah.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.133
And so it's the best of the best
of the world.

00:08:33.133 --> 00:08:34.701
They've already been
on "Top Chef,"

00:08:34.701 --> 00:08:37.367
they've already won, or they've
already made it to the finale.

00:08:37.367 --> 00:08:38.467
-Wow.
So you're watching the best.

00:08:38.467 --> 00:08:39.868
I will say also --
-It's like the Olympics.

00:08:39.868 --> 00:08:41.000
It's like "Top Chef" Olympics.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:42.501
-"Top Chef"
is one of those shows, too,

00:08:42.501 --> 00:08:45.100
where the winners actually go on
to become giant stars.

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:46.334
-Yeah.

00:08:46.334 --> 00:08:47.701
-They have restaurants.
They have franchises.

00:08:47.701 --> 00:08:49.634
They're like giants now
in the culinary world.

00:08:49.634 --> 00:08:52.567
-Yeah. Hell yeah. I mean, you
can look at any show you want --

00:08:52.567 --> 00:08:54.200
you know, "American idol,"

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:55.968
any show,
any reality competition show --

00:08:55.968 --> 00:09:00.634
and no show produces genuine
captains of their industry.

00:09:00.634 --> 00:09:02.901
And they -- I think
the show is self-selecting,

00:09:02.901 --> 00:09:04.534
you know,
because it's so hard to do.

00:09:04.534 --> 00:09:05.901
-Yeah.
-And you've got to be insane

00:09:05.901 --> 00:09:07.100
to want to do it.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:08.434
I would never compete
on "Top Chef."

00:09:08.434 --> 00:09:09.601
-Really?
-But -- Yes.

00:09:09.601 --> 00:09:11.133
It's even harder
than it looks on TV.

00:09:11.133 --> 00:09:13.601
And you've been on the show,
but you weren't in the kitchen.

00:09:13.601 --> 00:09:16.200
But you were eating with us.
-No, I was --

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:18.033
Yeah, they left me outside
in the parking lot.

00:09:18.033 --> 00:09:19.501
Yeah, they go --
-"You just stay here."

00:09:19.501 --> 00:09:21.434
-"We'll bring the food to you,
Jimmy. You stay in the park--"

00:09:21.434 --> 00:09:23.434
But -- Oh, it's tough.

00:09:23.434 --> 00:09:25.501
-It was --
I mean, it's great, you know?

00:09:25.501 --> 00:09:27.100
-Carla was my --
was the winner of mine.

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:28.300
-Oh, really?
-And she went on --

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:29.934
-And look how well she's done.
-She's the best.

00:09:29.934 --> 00:09:31.300
-Carla Hall.
-We love you, Carla.

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:34.000
-I mean, the Voltaggio Brothers.
Richard Blais.

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:35.767
-Richard Blais is great.
-Stephanie Izard.

00:09:35.767 --> 00:09:37.200
Kristen Kish.
-Yeah, it's amazing.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:38.434
-I can keep naming people
that we all know now.

00:09:38.434 --> 00:09:39.934
-I want to show a clip.

00:09:39.934 --> 00:09:42.100
Here's Padma Lakshmi in
"Top Chef: World All-Stars."

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:43.334
Take a look at this.

00:09:43.334 --> 00:09:45.067
-Hello, Chefs!

00:09:45.067 --> 00:09:48.934
Welcome to season 20
of "Top Chef."

00:09:48.934 --> 00:09:50.000
-Alright!

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:52.601
[ Applause ]

00:09:52.601 --> 00:09:55.634
-Since "Top Chef" premiered
in 2006,

00:09:55.634 --> 00:09:59.000
there have been
29 international versions,

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:02.934
with over 100 winners
from around the globe.

00:10:02.934 --> 00:10:06.434
You represent some of
the best of the best.

00:10:06.434 --> 00:10:10.434
-I recognize Samuel, because I
always watch "Top Chef: France"

00:10:10.434 --> 00:10:12.300
and I know he's a great chef.

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:14.133
This competition's
going to be fire.

00:10:14.133 --> 00:10:16.901
-Oh, yeah.
Padma Lakshmi, our bud.

00:10:16.901 --> 00:10:19.834
"Top Chef: World All-Stars"
airs Thursdays

00:10:19.834 --> 00:10:21.667
at 9:00 p.m. on Bravo.

00:10:21.667 --> 00:10:24.167
We're doing something brand-new
with Padma after the break.

00:10:24.167 --> 00:10:25.801
Stick around, everybody.

